---
import MainLayout from "../layout/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout title="Jakub Olszewski's about">
  <div class="max-w-185 mx-auto px-8 py-20">
    <p class="font-mono text-s text-(--accent) mb-3">About</p>
    <section>
      <section
        class="p-4 bg-(--surface) mb-10 border border-(--border) rounded-md overflow-hidden"
      >
        <h2
          class="mb-3 font-sans text-4xl border-l-2 border-(--accent) pl-3"
        >
          What I Build
        </h2>
        <p class="font-mono">
          Most of what I've been working on has been made with JavaScript. Both
          the component driven frontends and the APIs behind them. I'm more
          comfortable on the frontend, but I am actively looking to improve
          myself across the stack.
        </p>
        <br />
        <p>I work with: </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mt-4 mb-4">
          {
            [
              "HTML",
              "CSS",
              "JavaScript",
              "React",
              "NextJS",
              "Astro",
              "Node.js",
              "Express",
              "MongoDB",
              'Python',
              "Figma",
              "Illustrator",
              "Photoshop",
            ].map((t) => <span class="pill">{t}</span>)
          }
        </div>
      </section>

      <section
        class="p-4 bg-(--surface) mb-10 border border-(--border) rounded-md overflow-hidden"
      >
        <h2
          class="mb-3 font-sans text-4xl border-l-2 border-(--accent) pl-3"
        >
          How I Work
        </h2>
        <p class="font-mono">
          I try not to overthink my code so that it is simple and easy to
          follow, not just for me but for my colleagues and whoever reads it
          next. I care about accessibility, sustainability browser consistency
          and not overcomplicating things.
        </p>
        <br />
        <p class="font-mono">
          I'm finishing my degree and these projects represent where I am right
          now. I don't have years of production experience yet, but I'm serious
          about the craft and keen to keep improving.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section
        class="p-4 bg-(--surface) mb-10 border border-(--border) rounded-md overflow-hidden"
      >
        <h2
          class="mb-3 font-sans text-4xl border-l-2 border-(--accent) pl-3"
        >
          Experience
        </h2>
        <p class="font-mono">
          Before finishing my degree I did an internship as a Datacenter
          Operations Engineer at a ByteDance datacenter. It was a different side
          of the industry from web development, physical infrastructure,
          operations, keeping things running at scale, breakfix and datacenter
          operations. I came away with a letter of recommendation and a much
          better understanding of what sits underneath the software I build.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section
        class="p-4 bg-(--surface) border border-(--border) rounded-md overflow-hidden"
      >
        <h2
          class="mb-3 font-sans text-4xl border-l-2 border-(--accent) pl-3"
        >
          Let's Connect
        </h2>
        <p class="font-mono">
          Always happy to chat or hear about new opportunities.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 flex flex-col gap-1">
          <li>
            <a
            target="_blank"
              href="https://github.com/Jakubo0451"
              class="font-mono text-sm text-(--muted) hover:text-(--accent) transition-colors"
              >GitHub ↗</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
            target="_blank"
              href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/jakub-olszewski-43922534a/"
              class="font-mono text-sm text-(--muted) hover:text-(--accent) transition-colors"
              >LinkedIn ↗</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              href="mailto:jakubolszewski451@gmail.com"
              class="font-mono text-sm text-(--muted) hover:text-(--accent) transition-colors"
              >Email ↗</a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </section>
  </div>
</MainLayout>
